   "ALMOST NOTHING, BUT NOT NOTHING HOW EMPTY IS EMPTY? 1 atom per cubic centimeter: typical interstellar gas 10¹⁹ molecules per cubic centimeter in the air you breathe The interstellar medium (ISM) is about 99% gas & 1% dust, by mass. It is mostly hydrogen & helium, like the stars. Spread over the whole galaxy, it adds up to about 15% of the mass of the stars. New stars form from it; dying stars return gas & dust to it (Deck 17).",
