   "VOYAGER CROSSES THE LINE PART 2  ·  THE SUN'S BUBBLE 1977 Voyager 1 & 2 launch Dec 2004 Voyager 1 crosses the termination shock (94 AU) Aug 2007 Voyager 2 crosses the termination shock (84 AU) Aug 25, 2012 Voyager 1 crosses the heliopause (121.6 AU) Nov 5, 2018 Voyager 2 crosses the heliopause (119 AU) Voyager 1's sign: the plasma around it became about 40 times denser.",
   "ONE LIGHT-DAY AWAY PART 2  ·  THE SUN'S BUBBLE 24 h one-way radio time to Voyager 1 around Nov 18, 2026 At that point Voyager 1 is about 25.9 billion km from Earth. A question & its answer take two full days to go there & back. Its power supply weakens every year, so NASA turns off instruments to save energy. It is still sending data from interstellar space.",
