   "ECCENTRICITY TELLS THE STORY PART 3  ·  VISITORS FROM OTHER STARS Eccentricity (e) = a number that tells how stretched an orbit is e = 0: a circle. Between 0 & 1: an ellipse, so the object is bound to the Sun. e above 1: a hyperbola. The object passes through once & leaves forever. All three visitors had e above 1 & arrived too fast to belong to our Sun.",
