   "TODAY I CAN… rank claims from proven to fiction & explain why NGSS Practice 7 use the Evidence Meter: EF, PH, IS & UK NGSS Practice 7 tell what makes a claim scientific NGSS Practice 7 explain why fast-spinning galaxies hint at dark matter ES.1.5 · Deck 18 link describe how lensing maps mass we cannot see ES.1.1 compare the dark matter suspects enrichment weigh dark matter against changing gravity (MOND) NGSS Practice 7 explain how supernovae showed the speed-up ES.1.2 compare a constant dark energy with a changing one ES.1.2 · enrichment rank the possible endings of the universe ES.1.2 split black-hole facts from black-hole guesses ES.1.4 describe how scientists test a wild idea NGSS Practice 7",
   "THE EVIDENCE METER THE TOOL FOR THIS WHOLE UNIT Every claim in Decks 21 to 24 gets one of these four labels. ESTABLISHED FACT Tested many ways by many teams. It could still change, but only with big new evidence. e.g. the universe is expanding (Deck 19) PLAUSIBLE HYPOTHESIS Testable, with some evidence for it, but not confirmed. Scientists still argue about it. e.g. inflation; dark energy may change over time INFORMED SPECULATION Fits known physics, but has little or no evidence yet. Often very hard to test today. e.g. wormholes you could travel through UNKNOWN Nobody knows yet, or the evidence is disputed. e.g. what dark matter is made of most evidence least evidence",
   "WHAT MAKES A CLAIM SCIENTIFIC? HOW SCIENCE WORKS A wild idea can still be science, if it passes these three checks. Testable It makes a prediction you could check with an observation or experiment. ESTABLISHED FACT Falsifiable Some result could prove it wrong. If nothing could ever prove it wrong, it is not science. ESTABLISHED FACT Checked by others Experts review the methods before it is published, and other teams try to repeat it. ESTABLISHED FACT",
   "PART 1 Dark Matter Something we cannot see is pulling on everything we can. How do you weigh something invisible?",
   "GALAXIES SPIN TOO FAST PART 1  ·  DARK MATTER 1970 Vera Rubin & Kent Ford measure how fast Andromeda's stars orbit Stars far from a galaxy's center orbit about as fast as stars near the center. ESTABLISHED FACT The visible stars and gas do not have enough gravity to hold those fast outer stars. ESTABLISHED FACT So something extra is pulling: unseen mass, or gravity that works differently. ESTABLISHED FACT",
   "MASS BENDS LIGHT: THE BULLET CLUSTER PART 1  ·  DARK MATTER Gravitational lensing = mass bends the light from objects behind it, like a giant lens Einstein's general relativity predicted light bending; the 1919 solar eclipse measured it. ESTABLISHED FACT In the Bullet Cluster, two galaxy clusters collided. Lensing shows most mass is offset from the hot gas. ESTABLISHED FACT Best explanation: dark matter passed straight through the crash while the gas slowed down. (strongly supported) PLAUSIBLE HYPOTHESIS",
   "ABOUT 5 TIMES MORE DARK MATTER THAN ATOMS PART 1  ·  DARK MATTER 27% : 5% dark matter vs. ordinary matter, share of the universe (Planck 2018) Planck mapped tiny hot and cold spots in the cosmic microwave background (Deck 19). ESTABLISHED FACT The spot pattern fits only if there is about 5 times more dark matter than ordinary matter. (model-based) ESTABLISHED FACT Dark matter does not give off, absorb or reflect light. We see only its gravity. ESTABLISHED FACT",
   "WHAT IS IT? THE SUSPECTS PART 1  ·  DARK MATTER Many teams are hunting. Nobody has caught dark matter yet.",
   "OR IS GRAVITY DIFFERENT? PART 1  ·  DARK MATTER Same data, two explanations. Dark matter • unseen mass adds extra gravity • explains fast-spinning galaxies • explains the Bullet Cluster offset • explains the CMB spot pattern (favored) PLAUSIBLE HYPOTHESIS MOND (Milgrom, 1983) • gravity changes when pulls are very weak • fits many galaxy rotation curves well • struggles with galaxy clusters • struggles with the Bullet Cluster (disfavored) PLAUSIBLE HYPOTHESIS",
   "PART 1  ·  DARK MATTER CHECK FOR UNDERSTANDING: PART 1 In the Bullet Cluster, most mass sits away from the hot gas. What does that observation show? A Something unseen holds most of the mass B Dark matter is made of WIMPs C Gravity does not work in clusters D The gas is heavier than everything else",
   "PART 2 Dark Energy Something is making the universe's expansion speed up. If gravity pulls everything together, why is expansion getting faster?",
   "THE EXPANSION IS SPEEDING UP PART 2  ·  DARK ENERGY 1929 Hubble: distant galaxies move away. The universe is expanding. ESTABLISHED FACT 1998 Two teams: far-away Type Ia supernovae are dimmer than expected. ESTABLISHED FACT 2011 Nobel Prize to Perlmutter, Schmidt & Riess for the speed-up. ESTABLISHED FACT 2025 DESI maps 14 million galaxies: hints that dark energy changes. PLAUSIBLE HYPOTHESIS 'Dark energy' is the name for whatever causes the speed-up. What it is: UNKNOWN",
   "CONSTANT OR CHANGING? PART 2  ·  DARK ENERGY Dark energy is about 68% of the universe's energy (Planck 2018). (model-based) ESTABLISHED FACT A cosmological constant • the same strength everywhere, forever • Einstein's 'Lambda' • the simplest fit for 25 years PLAUSIBLE HYPOTHESIS Dark energy that changes • its strength changes over time • DESI 2025: 2.8 to 4.2 sigma preference • a 'discovery' in physics needs 5 sigma (not confirmed) PLAUSIBLE HYPOTHESIS",
   "HOW DOES IT ALL END? PART 2  ·  DARK ENERGY Big Freeze The universe expands forever. Stars burn out. Everything gets cold and dark. (favored) PLAUSIBLE HYPOTHESIS Big Rip Dark energy grows stronger and tears apart galaxies, then stars, then atoms. INFORMED SPECULATION Big Crunch The expansion stops and reverses. Everything falls back together. INFORMED SPECULATION",
   "PART 2  ·  DARK ENERGY CHECK FOR UNDERSTANDING: PART 2 DESI found a 3-sigma hint that dark energy changes. Which label fits best right now? A Established fact B Plausible hypothesis C Informed speculation D Unknown",
